Tom: I''d like to talk about Tu Youyou. She discovered a new medicine for malaria.
Lily: Oh, the scientist who won the Nobel Prize? Why do you admire her?
Tom: Because she never gave up. Her team failed many times before they succeeded.
Lily: That''s true. I think I''ll choose Florence Nightingale.
Tom: The nurse? Why her?
Lily: She cared for wounded soldiers and founded modern nursing. She was very brave.
Tom: Great choice. Both of them helped a lot of people.', '老师让谈一位敬佩的人。Tom 选屠呦呦,因为她发现治疟疾的新药、屡败屡战从不放弃;Lily 选南丁格尔,因为她照料伤兵、创立现代护理、很勇敢。两人都帮助了许多人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who does Tom choose to talk about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Tu Youyou.","Florence Nightingale.","Einstein.","Lu Xun."]},{"q":"Why does Tom admire her?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She was very rich.","She never gave up after failing.","She was famous in films.","She lived very long."]},{"q":"Who does Lily choose?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Florence Nightingale.","Tu Youyou.","Zhong Nanshan.","Einstein."]},{"q":"What did Lily''s person do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She discovered a new medicine.","She cared for soldiers and founded nursing.","She wrote famous novels.","She built bridges."]},{"q":"What do Tom and Lily agree about the two people?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Both were scientists.","Both lived in England.","Both helped many people.","Both won the Nobel Prize."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1');
But Einstein once said we should become a person of value, not just a person of success.
This means that helping others matters more than fame or money.
A kind teacher or a brave doctor can be great in a quiet way.
Greatness, then, is really about caring and never giving up.', '听到''伟大''我们常想到名人;但爱因斯坦说要做有价值的人,而非只追求成功;这意味着帮助别人比名利更重要;善良的老师、勇敢的医生也能以平凡的方式伟大;伟大其实关乎关爱和永不放弃。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do people often think of when they hear ''great''?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Money only.","Animals.","Cars.","Famous people."]},{"q":"What did Einstein say we should become?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A person of value, not just success.","The richest person.","A famous actor.","A quiet person."]},{"q":"What matters more than fame or money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Winning prizes.","Helping others.","Travelling far.","Being noticed."]},{"q":"Who can be great in a quiet way?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only scientists.","Only leaders.","A kind teacher or a brave doctor.","Only writers."]},{"q":"What is greatness really about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Being rich.","Being on television.","Living a long life.","Caring and never giving up."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1');
Guest: Of course. The team read more than two thousand old Chinese medical texts.
Host: Two thousand? That sounds like a huge amount of work.
Guest: It was. They also tested hundreds of plants, but at first nothing worked.
Host: So what was the key to success?
Guest: They drew out the extract at a lower temperature, and then it finally worked.
Host: Amazing. How many times did they fail before that?
Guest: More than a hundred and ninety times. They never gave up.', '主持人请教授讲新疟疾药如何被发现。团队读了两千多部中医古籍、测试数百种植物,起初都无效;关键是在较低温度提取提取物才成功;在此之前失败了190多次,但从不放弃。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How many old texts did the team read?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["More than two thousand.","Only ten.","About fifty.","None at all."]},{"q":"What happened when they first tested the plants?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Everything worked at once.","Nothing worked at first.","They stopped the project.","They lost the texts."]},{"q":"What was the key to success?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Reading more books.","Boiling at high heat.","Drawing out the extract at a lower temperature.","Using more plants."]},{"q":"How many times did they fail?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Twice.","Ten times.","Fifty times.","More than 190 times."]},{"q":"What does the guest say about the team''s spirit?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They never gave up.","They gave up quickly.","They worked alone.","They were not patient."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1');
During a dangerous outbreak, he stayed calm and told the public the truth.
He insisted on treating the most serious patients himself.
Years later, even in his eighties, he stepped forward to help again.
His courage and honesty make him a model of a great person.', '钟南山是许多中国人深深信任的医生;危险爆发期间他保持冷静、说出真相;坚持亲自救治最重的病人;多年后年逾八旬仍挺身相助;他的勇气与诚实使他成为伟人的典范。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How do many people in China feel about Zhong Nanshan?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They are afraid of him.","They deeply trust him.","They have never heard of him.","They dislike him."]},{"q":"What did he do during the dangerous outbreak?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He hid at home.","He left the country.","He stayed calm and told the truth.","He stopped working."]},{"q":"Which patients did he insist on treating?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The easiest ones.","Only children.","None at all.","The most serious ones."]},{"q":"What did he do years later in his eighties?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He stepped forward to help again.","He retired completely.","He refused to help.","He moved abroad."]},{"q":"What makes him a model of a great person?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His wealth.","His courage and honesty.","His fame on TV.","His long holidays."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1');
Ben: First, choose a person and say why he or she is great.
Anna: Okay. Then what should I write about?
Ben: Tell an impressive story from the person''s life. Stories make readers care.
Anna: Should I describe what the person looks like too?
Ben: Yes, a little. Describe the appearance and the personality.
Anna: And how should I end it?
Ben: Sum up how you feel about the person. That makes a strong ending.', 'Anna 要写敬佩之人的介绍却不知如何开头。Ben 建议:先选人并说明为何伟大;再讲一个动人的生平故事;适当描写外貌和性格;最后总结自己对此人的感受作为有力结尾。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Anna''s problem?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She has no paper.","She can''t read.","She doesn''t know how to start writing.","She lost her pen."]},{"q":"What does Ben say to do first?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Draw a picture.","Copy a book.","Write the ending.","Choose a person and say why they are great."]},{"q":"Why does Ben suggest telling a story?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because stories make readers care.","To make it longer.","To use big words.","To fill the page."]},{"q":"What does Ben say about describing the person?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Never describe them.","Describe the appearance and personality.","Only describe their clothes.","Describe only the face."]},{"q":"How should Anna end the introduction?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["By stopping suddenly.","By asking a question.","By summing up how she feels.","By repeating the title."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U1');
He said we should try not to become a person of success, but a person of value.
In other words, do not work only for fame or money.
Instead, do something good and useful for other people.
If we live this way, our lives will truly have meaning.', '这是爱因斯坦的一句名言:不要只想成为成功的人,而要做有价值的人;换句话说,别只为名利而努力;要为他人做一些有益的事;若这样生活,我们的人生才真正有意义。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Whose saying is this?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Tu Youyou''s.","Lu Xun''s.","Florence Nightingale''s.","Albert Einstein''s."]},{"q":"What kind of person should we try to become?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A person of value.","The richest person.","A famous singer.","A quiet person."]},{"q":"What should we NOT work only for?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Friends.","Fame or money.","Health.","Family."]},{"q":"What should we do instead?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Rest all day.","Travel far.","Do something good for others.","Buy more things."]},{"q":"What will happen if we live this way?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["We will become poor.","We will be forgotten.","Nothing will change.","Our lives will truly have meaning."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U1');

